  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#42436\", \"PowerToys#45077\", \"PowerToys#42531\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed many times before. Light Switch can't change the wallpaper with the theme yet. The other tickets were closed as duplicates of PowerToys#42436, so that ticket is the one to follow and add your use case to. A contributor said in that ticket (PowerToys#42436) that they had a prototype for wallpaper switching and linked it to PR #42624. I couldn't find that PR in the archive, so I can't tell you whether it was merged. Until it ships, you can use a separate tool that switches the wallpaper with the theme. One commenter suggested Auto Dark Mode, which does this. WinDynamicDesktop was also mentioned.\"}",
